From 88016e929befac09c91648602f884df0cd37bded Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rafael Bachmann <rafael.bachmann.93@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 13:43:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(configuration): servers of one's own

`SignalServers::Custom` carries a full `ServiceConfiguration`, so a store
registered against a test server stays self-describing. The configuration
serializes in a form a file can hold (URLs, CA PEM, trust roots and
zkgroup parameters as base64). Contact discovery, which runs in Signal's
enclaves, reports itself unavailable there.

Assisted-by: anthropic/claude-fable-5-1
